| DNA-damage model | MGM (Bertolet 2023) called per condensed-history nucleus crossing; track-length / chord-length correction `D_AB / l̄` with `l̄ = 2d/3` | Same MGM (cell-scale) via the public Python library; no chord correction needed because we evaluate at scalar yF values, not condensed-history tracks. |
| N_MDS(yF) | `0.13·yF + 9.66×10⁻⁴·yF²` (fitted to TOPAS-nBio) | Same functional form, library coefficients `(0.12962, 9.657×10⁻⁴)`; <0.3 % rel. err. vs paper-quoted. |
| Gamma complexity `f(C; yF)` | Gamma PDF with quadratic a(yF), b(yF) (fits in SI section 1.1.2, not retrieved) | Library's published quadratics: `a(yF)=8.41e-5·yF²+7.31e-3·yF+1.404`, `b(yF)=-6.62e-5·yF²+1.48e-3·yF+1.494`. |
